{number: 151}
{title: God Is Our Refuge Safe}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] God is our refuge safe, strength,
And our [C] present [G] aid, ever near us,
[D7] Therefore, tho' the earth be moved,
Hills midst the seas be east,
We will [G] not fear at all, For God is nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Al-[G] though the nations raged,
Although the [C] kingdoms [G] moved, conflicts swelling
[D7] Before His mighty word,
From war the nations cease,
The [G] troubled earth is stilled when voice is heard.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [G] come behold the works,
Jehovah's [C] hand has [G] wrought on the earth here,
To [D7] utmost ends of all He causes war to cease,
He makes abiding peace in [G] every land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Be [G] still and bow in fear
And know that [C] He is [G] God, all ye nations;
To [D7] us the Lord of Hosts ever our refuge be,
A refuge strong and sure is [G] our God.
{end_of_verse}
